The screenshot above shows the density function of the gamma distribution with the parameters Alpha
= 3 and Beta = 5.5. The most random numbers occur in the vicinity of the apex of the density function
(random number x = 11). This value is called the modal value. When you build the mean of many
realizations of this distribution, you will notice that the mean value is substantially greater than the mode/
